  "html": "<yesno-view modelid=\"63abefe2d3d5f7025c32a29b\" class=\"is-full\" sgpulse-type=\"component\"><template shadowroot=\"open\"><div class=\"component\"><div class=\"yesno-inner component__inner\"><div data-socialgoodpulse-id=\"63abefe2d3d5f7025c32a29b\" class=\"component__inner yesno__inner component is-question yesno 63abefe2d3d5f7025c32a29b  is-full    can-show-feedback can-show-marking \"><div class=\"component__header-container\"><base-view type=\"component\" lowercase_component=\"yesNo\" customclass=\"\"><template shadowroot=\"open\"><div class=\"component__header-wrapper  \"><div class=\"component__header yesNo__header\"><div class=\"component__header-inner yesNo__header-inner\"><div class=\"component__content\"><div tabindex=\"0\" class=\"component__body yesNo__body\"><div class=\"component__body-inner yesNo__body-inner\"><p>Availability refers to the need to make data accessible to all authorized users whenever they need it. Cyberattacks and system failures can prevent access to information, systems, and services.</p><p><strong>Can you identify the common causes of system failures that can impact the availability of data?</strong></p><p>When you select ‘Start,' you will be presented with a series of options. Tap ‘Yes’ if you think this could cause system failures that can impact the availability of information, systems, and services. If not, tap ‘No.'</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></template></base-view></div><div class=\"component__widget \"><div class=\"yesno_container \"><div class=\"yesno_question_container\" aria-describedby=\"_ItemLevelFeedback\" tabindex=\"-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><img class=\"current_question img_question\" aria-describedby=\"_ItemLevelFeedback\" src=\"./courses/ff9e491c-49be-4734-803e-a79e6e83dab1/01afc700-aa8e-52ba-afe5-2ffc14252051/en-US/assets/d2cc1479f4b746e2b22999ad08eadcf8.png\" alt=\"Equipment failure\"></img></div><div class=\"start_btn_container\"><button class=\"start_button\" aria-label=\"Click Start\"><